    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0676" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5061</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Russia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-09T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1474. Your 1216, April 24, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d511-f1"/> and 1321, May
                    25, 5 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d511-f2"/> Shipping Board advise that utmost is
                    being done to secure vessels for Archangel trade; that steamers <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nassovia</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Portonia</hi>
                    already in Archangel service; that board is in daily communication with Russian
                    commercial attaché, who has submitted list of requirements; and that it has been
                    policy of board to dispatch ships as they come from repair yards to France,
                    Italy and Russia, share and share alike.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
